Fix Firestore addDoc error:
"Unsupported field value: undefined (found in field iconBg ...)".

Requirement:
- Firestore must never receive `undefined` values in any document.
- Before calling addDoc/updateDoc/setDoc, sanitize the payload:
  - Remove keys whose value is `undefined`
  - Also recursively sanitize nested objects/arrays (in case future fields become nested)
- For iconBg specifically:
  - If it is missing/undefined, set a safe default (e.g. "#EF4444" or reuse brandColor)
  - Or omit it entirely if it's optional (preferred: default to brandColor to keep UI consistent)

Implement:
1) Add a helper in lib/firestoreSanitize.ts:

export function sanitizeForFirestore<T>(obj: T): T {
  if (obj === undefined) return undefined as any;
  if (obj === null) return obj as any;
  if (Array.isArray(obj)) {
    return obj
      .map(sanitizeForFirestore)
      .filter(v => v !== undefined) as any;
  }
  if (typeof obj === "object") {
    const out: any = {};
    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(obj as any)) {
      const sv = sanitizeForFirestore(v as any);
      if (sv !== undefined) out[k] = sv;
    }
    return out;
  }
  return obj as any;
}

2) In project creation code:
- Build projectData
- Ensure iconBg is set:
  projectData.iconBg = projectData.iconBg ?? projectData.brandColor ?? "#EF4444";
- Then:
  await addDoc(collection(db, "users", uid, "projects"), sanitizeForFirestore(projectData));

3) Also apply sanitizeForFirestore to updateProject and any other Firestore writes in the app.

4) Improve error UX:
- If addDoc throws, show the actual error message in UI and console.error(error).

After changes, verify:
- Create Project works even if iconBg is not provided.
- The project appears immediately in users/{uid}/projects in Firestore and in UI list.

