Here is the implementation of the Lead Capture Flow and Phone Field Upgrade.

### Changed/Added Files

1.  **`lib/countries.ts`** (New): Contains the ordered list of countries (Kuwait, Saudi, GCC, Arab, Rest of World) with flags and dial codes.
2.  **`components/PhoneInput.tsx`** (New): Reusable component with country selector and E.164 formatting.
3.  **`lib/leadStore.ts`** (New): Logic for managing leads, claims, and Firestore interactions.
4.  **`pages/Signup.tsx`**: Updated to use `PhoneInput` and E.164 format.
5.  **`components/ProjectWizard.tsx`**: Updated to support `isLeadMode`, replacing the signup step with a simplified contact form and saving to `leads` collection.
6.  **`pages/LeadCapture.tsx`** (New): Public route for the wizard.
7.  **`pages/admin/AdminLeads.tsx`** (New): Admin dashboard for managing leads.
8.  **`pages/ClaimProject.tsx`** (New): Route for converting a lead token into a real project/user.
9.  **`components/admin/AdminLayout.tsx`**: Added "Leads" navigation item.
10. **`App.tsx`**: Added new routes.

### Firestore Security Rules (Recommendation)

```text
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {

    // ... existing rules ...

    // LEADS: Public write (create), Admin read/write
    match /leads/{leadId} {
      allow create: if true; // Public lead capture
      allow read, update, delete: if request.auth != null && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/admins/$(request.auth.uid)).data.status == 'Active';
    }

    // CLAIM TOKENS: Public read (validate), Admin create/write
    match /lead_claim_tokens/{tokenId} {
      allow read: if true; // Needed to validate token on /claim page
      allow write: if request.auth != null && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/admins/$(request.auth.uid)).data.status == 'Active';
    }
  }
}
```

